":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"subscribed","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2020-02-19T10:08:09Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/588155526","html_url":"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/7276#issuecomment-588155526","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/7276","id":588155526,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU4ODE1NTUyNg==","user":{"login":"stuartwdouglas","id":328571,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyODU3MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/328571?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartwdouglas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-02-19T10:42:00Z","updated_at":"2020-02-19T10:42:00Z","body":"So the issue here is the use of CompletableFuture.runAsync. This uses the fork join pool which does not provide any way to set the context class loader, so if you attempt to load a service it will use the wrong CL.\r\n\r\nI am still trying to figure out a way to resolve this, but I can't really see any except for nasty hacks that may stop working in future versions of Java.\r\n\r\nYou can work around this by calling Thread.currentThread().setContextClassLoader(DoKubernetesRequestOnStartService.class.getClassLoader()); at the start of the async task.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/588155526/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"stuartwdouglas","id":328571,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyODU3MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/328571?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartwdouglas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartwdouglas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/588159288","html_url":"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/7276#issuecomment-588159288","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/7276","id":588159288,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU4ODE1OTI4OA==","user":{"login":"andreas-repp","id":9267365,"node